{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2774 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "275ef302f1c1c441809d0bb6ead00e3128feafef2b7b0dfa1b0c0d7d7079bb99" :edb/db-before-t 2773 :edb/db-after-t 2774 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536086 50 "2026-10-16T01:08:41.969Z" 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186051752 1078 17592186051754 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186051965 1078 17592186051967 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186051968 1078 17592186051969 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186051971 1078 17592186051973 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186054642 1038 17592186565446 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186054644 1038 17592186565456 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186055037 1070 17592186045485 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186055037 1071 "$2$ is prime, **or** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ **and** $5.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $R:2\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $S:14\\text{ is a multiple of }7$\n\n- $T:14\\text{ is a multiple of }5$" 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186055037 1071 "> $2$ is prime, **or** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ **and** $5$.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $R: 2is prime$\n- $S: 14is a multiple of7$\n- $T: 14is a multiple of5$" 13194139536086 17592186045417 false] [17592186055037 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $2$ is prime. This corresponds to $R.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $14$ is a multiple of $7$ and $5.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7}_{⏟}}_{S}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }5}_{⏟}}_{T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $S∧T.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{2\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{R}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{14\\text{ is a multiple of }7\\text{ and }5}_{⏟}}_{S\\,∧\\,T},\n$$\n\nthat is, $R∨(S∧T).$" 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186055087 1070 17592186045485 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186055087 1071 "$$\n{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $A$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $B$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186055087 1071 "$2pis negative_(⏟)_(A)por_(⏟)_(∨)0.5pis rational_(⏟)_(B)$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$A$ is {{field-1}},\n$B$ is {{field-2}},\n$A∨B$ is {{field-3}}." 13194139536086 17592186045417 false] [17592186055087 1074 "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $A$ is false, and $B$ is true. Therefore, the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{2\\text{ is negative}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{0.5\\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B} & \\,\\,≡\\,\\text{false}∨\\text{true}≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186096614 1038 17592186565449 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186096616 1038 17592186565467 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186096616 1038 17592186565474 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186096753 1038 17592186565437 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186096755 1038 17592186565457 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186096755 1038 17592186565482 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186105739 1038 17592186565452 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186105741 1038 17592186565454 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186105741 1038 17592186565459 13194139536086 17592186045417 true] [17592186116561 1075 17592186116562 13194139536086 17592186045417 false] [175